 in Co-op  it's great should you complete Far Cry 5  story then you should jump into Far Cry  New Dawn 17 years after the apocalyptic  events foreseen by Joseph seed the world  has changed Nature has taken back the US  and new villains are in charge large  twins Lou and Mickey are the antagonists  and their band of Highwaymen New Dawn  introduces a weapon crafting system as  the modern world is thrown back to the  Dark Ages but wait there's more Far Cry  Primal is also here taking the series  all the way back to the Stone Age we  play as a seasoned hunter-gatherer born  to survive in this unforgiving world but  there's no vehicles here so we have to  use saber-toothed tigers and bears  instead of course Primal is built on Far  Cry 4's engine not Far Cry 5 so it  doesn't feel as refined and responsive  as the other titles added today but it  does boast the highest average score of  all three which is just less than 8 out  of 10. next we can't have a PS plus  extra update without a Yakuza game well  there's three technically this time  first Yakuza like a dragon and don't  worry if you're having a bout of deja vu  right now like a dragon was on PS plus  essential only four months ago and the  defining difference between this and  most other Yakuza games is the fighting  system it's turn based this allows the  depth of options to shine through as you  beat someone round the Hedge with a snow  leopard or a bowl of fruit the options  in this game are strange the whole setup  is coming out of prison 18 years after  you were sent down and must reintegrate  with your Yakuza Underworld the second  Yakuza game this month is the Yakuza 6  the song of life touted as the final  installment of Kazuma kiru's story The  Fighting system in here is fully free no  turn-based action here and actually it's  been simplified so much it's far easier  to pick up and play than ever before the  story is about kiryu's last criminal  case to seek out a hit and run driver  who took the life of a family member as  that unwinds everything links back to  previous games and the Japanese Clans  and underworld Yakuza bosses in the  shadows if that's too sad for you don't  worry there's a cat cafe and you can  sing karaoke whenever you like finally  take a look at judgment a spin-off from  the Yakuza series we play as takayuki  Yagami a private investigator who is  desperate to clear his name the plot  revolves around a series of murders and  you are the only one who can find and  stop the culprit the psychological  Thriller storyline has been plotted by  many especially after the super silly  things that can happen in typical Yakuza  games will you try this one next we have  both Middle Earth games shadow of war  and Shadow of Mordor the best way to  describe these games is as Assassin's  Creed setting the Lord of the Rings  world the most amazing element in this  franchise is the Nemesis system that  generates your foes randomly as each are  faced your relationship with them  changes they may be fearful of your  Legend they may have heard about your  weaknesses and change the way they fight  since the last time you met this makes  replaying the game so much fun as those  enemies will most certainly be different  next time with new personalities and new  dialogue to discover chatting with  Gollum while keeping away from the Gaze  of Lord Sauron may not be completely in  keeping with the books but it's a good  time all the same how about an RPG that  is heavily inspired by the famous blood  bloodborne and Dark Souls franchises  mortal shell feels like an expansion to  those worlds with the same Aesthetics  and obtuse storytelling and shamelessly  runs with it battles are tense and  require timing to succeed or you'll get  used to seeing the fail screen many many  times if you like Trials of Will and  High Learning curves mortal shell may be  a good choice if you don't like  soulsborne games run away run away while  you can another RPG which couldn't be  more different is Adventure Time pirates  Jake and Finn travel the world in their  boat and take part in turn-based fights  the usual roles exist with tank support  and DPS and you must learn the best  combination to win the voice actors are  here from the TV show making the world  of Adventure Time more compelling and  Jake will even turn into different  vehicles to help speed up exploration  pillars of a 10 Unity II dead fire  completes the RPGs for the month and  this is more of a point-and-click  isometric RPG the themes are quite dark  we play as the Watcher a person who can  see into the souls of others lovely how  about a puzzle game check out The  Pedestrian we play as a stick drawing  tasked with moving from one street sign  to another the core mechanic is building  a level yourself and then running  through it your ability to put things in  the right place dictates how easy or  impossible the platforming element will  be the complexity builds up but it's  definitely manageable and you'll have it  done within five hours another puzzle  game this month is Evil Genius 2 world  domination imagine if you were grew in  Despicable Me and your minions would  complete tasks following your  instructions essentially Evil Genius 2  plays like a Sim game something like two  point campus just nothing near as good  next The Escapist 2 is an escape  simulator as we are locked up in prison  and we want to get out each day is  defined by routine picking times and  opportunities to find a way to escape is  your only interest from searching cells  while guards are looking the wrong way  to digging holes to Freedom get caught  and that hole will be filled back in and  you'll be back to square one worms wmd  is a turn-based war simulator but with  worms everything is set on a flat 2D  plane and each worm waits for their time  to have 30 seconds to either fight or  flee with countless power-ups it's a  total blast with friends the kids games  this month are Ben 10 Power Trip in  which we